//RS 
//RS // ── #2075: which profile a CLI behavior test pays for ────────────────────────
//RS //
//RS // D-LENS-RUN1 keeps the AOT escape hatch for ANY explicit profile, so
//RS // `jet run --profile=debug` still proves a real native build (I2/I5) — it just
//RS // stops paying `-O`/opt-level=3 + ThinLTO + symbol stripping (Source/main.rs
//RS // `ProfileConfig::rustc_args`, `OptimizeLevel::None`) for an assertion about
//RS // argument binding, diagnostics, process behavior, or a foreign binding's
//RS // output. Those tests use `--profile=debug`.
//RS //
//RS // `--release` stays ONLY where the release lens is what is under test. The
//RS // named keep set, in full:
//RS //
//RS //   cli_parts/expand.rs        `profile_release_flag_is_accepted`
//RS //                              (`--release` is a blessed profile, no E1219)
//RS //   cli_parts/budget.rs        `typed_cli_field_markers_add_short_and_env_
//RS //                              inputs_with_pinned_precedence` — runs its whole
//RS //                              precedence matrix for `release in [false, true]`,
//RS //                              which IS the default+release end-to-end proof
//RS //   cli_parts/core.rs          `jobs_lists_documented_scheduled_project_jobs_
//RS //                              and_matches_run_outside_projects` (`build
//RS //                              --release` strips `#Job` dev entries; a debug
//RS //                              build keeps them, so this needs release)
//RS //   cli_parts/inspect.rs       `hardened_release_sentry_reaches_a_foreign_
//RS //                              dependency` (hardened release sentry semantics)
//RS //
//RS // Everything else in the cli targets is behavior, and pays debug.
//RS 
