//RS /// Replace machine-specific temp paths so snapshots are portable.
//RS ///
//RS /// A diagnostic may render the entry as an absolute path, as a path relative to
//RS /// the temp root, or as the bare file name, and which one it picks is not this
//RS /// helper's business — its only job is to make the snapshot host-independent.
//RS /// Only the first two were normalized, so a diagnostic that rendered the bare
//RS /// name left a real machine-independent string that simply did not match the
//RS /// `BAD.jet` convention every other fixture in this suite uses, and the test
//RS /// read as a failure in the compiler rather than in the scrubber. This target
//RS /// sits outside every routine set (#2025), so nobody saw it.
//RS pub fn scrub(s: &str, file: &Path) -> String {
